v 3
d 'CROSSWALK_MULTICLASS': module providing crosswalk tables to translate ISCO-88com and ISCO-08 into the Multilevel Socio-Economic Classes schemes
d
d crosswalk_multiclass is an add-on for the crosswalk package by Ben
d Jann. It provides crosswalk tables translating ISCO-88com and ISCO-08
d occupational codes into the Multilevel Socio-Economic Classes (MSEC)
d schemes -- Micro-SEC (30 classes), Meso-SEC (18 classes), and Macro-SEC
d (11 classes, ESEC plus differentiation of SC I and II) -- plus, for
d ISCO-08 only, a separate 77-category micro-class scheme that is not
d part of MSEC. Micro-SEC, Meso-SEC and Macro-SEC are defined jointly
d over occupation and employment relation, so those tables carry one
d destination column per employment status, and two case functions are
d supplied to construct that argument; the micro-class scheme is purely
d occupational and takes no case. Tables are provided for 4-digit ISCO
d codes and, directly, for 3-digit ISCO minor groups. The MSEC schemes
d nest: Micro-SEC, Meso-SEC and Macro-SEC each aggregate to the European
d Socio-economic Classification (ESeC). This package does not duplicate
d plain ESeC itself, since crosswalk already provides isco88_to_esec()
d and isco08_to_esec(); see help crosswalk_multiclass for details and
d the correct case functions to use with them. The package contains no
d ado-file and defines no command of its own; all recoding is carried
d out by the crosswalk command.
d
d KW: ISCO-88com
d KW: ISCO-08
d KW: occupation
d KW: social class
d KW: ESeC
d KW: Macro-SEC
d KW: Micro-SEC
d KW: micro-class
d KW: Meso-SEC
d KW: MSEC
d KW: class scheme
d KW: crosswalk
d
d Requires: Stata version 14 and crosswalk, moremata from SSC (q.v.)
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260819
d
d Author: Oscar Smallenbroek
d
f crosswalk_multiclass.sthlp
f _cwcasefcn_mcempstat.sthlp
